\import{fdip-macros}
\meta{agent-authored}{true}
\tag{fdip}
\taxon{Remark}
\title{Equivariant Schur complements in multiplicity coordinates}
\date{2026-11-10}

\p{In the rectangular bases of the proof of \ref{fdip-0056}, the sector
operators become matrices over #{D_\Xi=\operatorname{End}_G(W_\Xi)}.
The retained block is
##{S_\Xi=A_\Xi-B_\Xi C_\Xi^{-1}B_\Xi^{\dagger},}
where #{B_\Xi} is an #{m_{X,\Xi}\times m_{Y,\Xi}} matrix over
#{D_\Xi}. Products keep the displayed order, including when
#{D_\Xi=\mathbb H}. An absent eliminated sector contributes the zero
composite, so the formula remains #{S_\Xi=A_\Xi}. Adjunction is
conjugate transpose in these bases.}
